"},{"type":"Domain","start":244,"end":544,"description":"Protein kinase"},{"type":"Binding site","start":250,"end":258,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":277,"end":277,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Active site","start":379,"end":379,"description":"Proton acceptor"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":409,"end":409,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":439,"end":567,"description":"Sufficient for interaction with CLU"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":548,"end":548,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":553,"end":553,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homodimer. Heterohexamer; TGFB1, TGFB2 and TGFB3 homodimeric ligands assemble a functional receptor composed of two TGFBR1 and TGFBR2 heterodimers to form a ligand-receptor heterohexamer. The respective affinity of TGFRB1 and TGFRB2 for the ligands may modulate the kinetics of assembly of the receptor and may explain the different biological activities of TGFB1, TGFB2 and TGFB3. Component of a complex composed of TSC22D1 (via N-terminus), TGFBR1 and TGFBR2; the interaction between TSC22D1 and TGFBR1 is inhibited by SMAD7 and promoted by TGFB1 (PubMed:21791611). Interacts with DAXX. Interacts with DYNLT4. Interacts with ZFYVE9; ZFYVE9 recruits SMAD2 and SMAD3 to the TGF-beta receptor. Interacts with and is activated by SCUBE3; this interaction does not affect TGFB1-binding to TGFBR2. Interacts with VPS39; this interaction is independent of the receptor kinase activity and of the presence of TGF-beta. Interacts with CLU (PubMed:8555189)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P37173-2","name":"2","synonyms":["betaR-IIB"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Has transforming growth factor beta-activated receptor activity"}],"length":592,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000359013.4"],"refseq":["NM_001024847.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001020018.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,31],[58,33,5